    "BodyPart": {
      "description": "Coarse body regions used by the optional `bone_mask` field on gestures.\n\nA gesture's bone_mask declares which limbs the action drives. Listeners\nuse this to reason about layering: a `wave` (right_arm only) can run\nconcurrently with a `walk_to` (full-body locomotion) without clobbering\nthe legs, while two right_arm actions at the same time conflict.\n\nValues are intentionally coarse (one per limb / region) so the LLM can\npick them by name without needing to know the underlying Mixamo bone\nnaming. The executor maps each part to its bones internally.",
      "enum": [
        "head",
        "spine",
        "left_arm",
        "right_arm",
        "left_leg",
        "right_leg",
        "face"
      ],
      "title": "BodyPart",
      "type": "string"
    },
